LearnAI environment variables
=============================

The root `.env.example` is a reference pointer only. The real values live in the
per-service env files, which `docker-compose.yml` reads via `env_file`:

    backend/.env      <- backend/.env.example
    frontend/.env     <- frontend/.env.example

Docker Compose additionally reads a root `.env` for `${...}` interpolation, so
point it at the backend file. That keeps the S3 credentials and the SeaweedFS
signing key in exactly one place:

    ln -sfn backend/.env .env

Without that symlink, `docker compose` fails with
"required variable MINIO_ACCESS_KEY is missing a value" — the compose file
deliberately refuses to fall back to a built-in credential.

To set up locally
-----------------

    cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
    cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
    ln -sfn backend/.env .env

Then edit backend/.env and fill in at least:

    DB_URL              postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/learnai
    JWT_SECRET          at least 32 characters; the backend refuses to boot otherwise
    GEMINI_API_KEY      for chat, quiz and mind-map generation
    COHERE_API_KEY      for embeddings, reranking and web search
    MINIO_ACCESS_KEY    SeaweedFS S3 account; required, no built-in default
    MINIO_SECRET_KEY    SeaweedFS S3 account; required, no built-in default
    SEAWEEDFS_JWT_SIGNING_KEY
                        SeaweedFS signing key; required, keep stable across restarts
    SUPABASE_URL        optional; only needed if you use Supabase Storage
    SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
                        optional; server-only, never expose to the browser
    RESEND_API_KEY      optional; sends the password-reset code by email.
                        Without it the code is written to the backend log instead
    MAIL_FROM           optional; must be a verified Resend sender
    ADMIN_EMAIL         optional; the bootstrap administrator. When set, the
                        backend creates the account on boot with ADMIN_PASS
                        as the initial password
    ADMIN_PASS          optional; the initial admin password, at least 6
                        characters. The admin can change it from the admin
                        console, and a restart never reverts that change
    ADMIN_NAME          optional; display name for the bootstrap admin

Generate each secret with:

    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"

Where to look
-------------

    backend/.env.example    every backend variable, with local defaults
    frontend/.env.example   the two public frontend variables

The frontend only ever sees NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables, which are inlined into the
browser bundle at build time. Changing them requires a rebuild, not just a
restart. See instruction.md for the full local setup and the Render/Vercel
deployment walkthrough.
